# Path to your Obsidian vault
NOTE_ROOT=/path/to/folder

# End-of-Wikipedia LLM reviewer (advisory second pass over the deterministic
# common-name extraction) via an external LLM backend. Runs by default when
# LLM_MODEL is set — there is no default model. There are two backends,
# selected with LLM_BACKEND:
#
# - opencode (default): remote models through the opencode V2 server, reached
#   via the `opencode api` CLI (which owns service discovery, auth, and
#   auto-start of the background service). LLM_MODEL is 'provider/model'
#   (e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5). API keys live in opencode itself
#   (`opencode auth login`) — never here. Leave OPENCODE_SERVER_URL unset to
#   use the shared background service; set it to pin a specific server (e.g.
#   http://localhost:4096). OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD authenticates against a
#   password-protected server.
# - ollama: local daemon (`ollama serve`). LLM_MODEL is a daemon model name,
#   e.g. `ollama pull qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M`.
#LLM_BACKEND=opencode
#OPENCODE_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4096
#OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=
#LLM_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:11434
#LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5
#LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=16000
# To disable the reviewer: set LLM_DISABLED=true or pass --no-review.
#LLM_DISABLED=true

# Review-gap tally log: LLM corrections are appended here so they can be
# promoted to regression tests via `npm run tally -- --regressions=3`.
#REVIEW_LOG_PATH=.review-data/review-gaps.jsonl
